purity:
Which way to my heart was the right way to go;
Unless in your purity, soul-clean and clear,
God whispers his messages into your ear.

purest:
Like the soul of Alice;
It of purest white is wrought,
Filled with gems of crystal thought.

purse:
Better and worse;
But put a silver penny in her purse,
Kissed Laura, crossed the heath with clumps of furze

pursue:
But see the softly-stealing tears apace
Pursue each other down the mourner's face;
But cease thy tears, bid ev'ry sigh depart,

purge:
This life is long, but yet it ends;
Repent and purge your soul and save:
No gladder song the morning stars

purty:
In dis world to swaller down;
An' ol' Sorrer 's purty lively
In her way o' gittin' roun'.

Dat's my gal;
Ain't she purty? goodness lan'!
Huh name Sal.

purhaps:
An' you 'se jes' a little tiahed
An' purhaps a little mad;
How yo' gloom tu'ns into gladness,

purloin:
'Good folk, I have no coin;
To take were to purloin:
I have no copper in my purse,

purging:
And with their blood washed their pollutions clean,
Purging the land which spewed them from its throat;
Their daughters took we for a pleasant prey,

purple's:
This Head has all the people for a heart;
This purple’s lined with the democracy,—
Now let him see to it! for a rent within

purposing:
The antithesis is human. Harken, dear;
There’s too much abstract willing, purposing,
In this poor world. We talk by aggregates,
